  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# v1.0.0 (ships with FiveFR 0.5.0b)\n- Rebuild addons against this API: CalloutPed.Speak now returns a Task, so older addon DLLs break.\n- Added SpawnSuspect / SpawnCivilian returning Suspect and Civilian wrappers (Status, Identity, Record,\n  Inventory, Blip, Move, Demeanor, On events). SpawnPed is obsolete.\n- Added SpawnCalloutVehicle and CalloutVehicle (WhenHere, Arrived) for vehicles spawned far from the officer.\n- Added awaitable Speak with SpeechVoice and a listener, plus Ped.Voice.\n- Added RadioApi: Radio replies with Say/Response, TransmitAsOfficer, Transmit and Callsign.\n- Added offense declarations for callouts, On.OfficerArrived with the officer's callsign, Demeanor and Tendency.\n- Added Ranks, RankStanding and the XP award events.\n- Added ConfigLayout and Configuration.ReplaceLoaded for the split config/ files.\n- Added DiagnosticLog, which stays out of F8 and shows in each addon's console in the MDT.\n- Added RandomHash (Ped, Animal, Vehicle, Weapon) and Vector4 location helpers.\n- Documented every public member. Corrected DispatchService.ArrivedRequirements and SceneFinishRequirements docs.\n- QueueLoop / QueueConditionalLoop accept an interval source read on every check.\n\n# v0.9.3\n- Made random helper methods public (Whoops!)\n- Added abstract class LinkedEvent\n- Added class InventoryItem\n- Added abstract class Plugin\n\n# v0.9.2\n- Added static DataContainer constructor for better data management use cases.\n- Added CalloutPriorityAttribute (required during admin-induced priority periods)\n- Added SelectRandom extensions for Dictionary and Array types.\n- Added new Ended boolean to the Callout class for detecting if a callout ended early.\n- Added new TryGetNextSeatFree extension for Vehicle types.\n\n# v0.9.1\n - Added summaries to API endpoints\n - Added QueueService\n\n# v0.9.0\n - Implemented License Validation Server and attributed premium features\n - Added new EntityExtensions",
